{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Suggested diligence questions—not a mandatory approval rule:\n\n- **Selection:** What criteria were used to choose the exchange and lead market maker (LMM)? Were alternatives compared on listing fees, distribution, trading quality, technology, and support? What conflicts or incentives could affect the choice?\n- **Relevant-market expertise:** What experience does the LMM have with ETFs of similar strategy, liquidity, underlying assets, and trading hours? How will it source or hedge inventory, manage spreads and volatility, and coordinate with authorized participants? What service levels, monitoring, escalation, and replacement rights apply?\n- **Capital and seed support:** What capital, inventory, or seed support is committed, by whom, for how long, and on what terms? Is support guaranteed or discretionary, and what happens if it ends or is withdrawn? Distinguish temporary LMM/affiliate market-making seed from durable investor assets: what evidence supports expected independent demand and asset retention after temporary support ends?"}}
